  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 42. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 告知 — 必要なことを知らせること。\n2. 克服 — 苦手なことや困難を乗り越えること。\n3. 国宝 — 特に価値が高い文化財として国が指定したもの。\n4. 国名 — 国の名前。\n5. 穀類 — 米や麦など主に種を食べる作物のなかま。\n6. 心当たり — 思い当たることや見当がつくこと。\n7. 心得 — 前もって知っておくべき事柄や心構え。\n8. 心がけ — いつも気をつけて大切にしようとする気持ち。\n9. 心構え — 物事に向き合うための心の準備。\n10. 志 — こうしようと心に決めた目標。\n11. 心遣い — 相手のことを思って気を配ること。\n12. 心待ち — 楽しみにしながら待つこと。\n13. 試み — うまくいくか実際にやってみること。\n14. 個室 — 一人や一組だけで使える部屋。\n15. 古書 — 昔に出版された本や使われた本。\n16. 小島 — 小さな島。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
